    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-7937",
      "problem": "Find the equation that generates the graph shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/10f082165ef5b901e0ec43139fac54317395e1b349b31dd491dc36980981a622.png)",
      "worked_solution": "To obtain the given graph, we perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the left by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+1}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/3561b98dcf8113dcb644b1f3c738821f74d9f453e268fb2d47f6379d41f31951.png)\n\nTherefore, the answer is $y=\\sqrt{x+1}.$",
